WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:01.901
[music playing]

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:02.936
GORDON RAMSAY (VOICEOVER):
I'm in Morocco, North Africa,

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:05.038
to discover the hidden
culinary secrets

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:08.308
of this incredible country.

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:11.044
I've always loved Moroccan
food because every bite

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:12.512
is steeped in history.

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:14.414
GORDON RAMSAY (VOICEOVER):
Over the centuries, the Arabs,

00:00:14.481 --> 00:00:16.583
Spanish, Ottomans,
and French have all

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:19.252
left their mark on the cuisine
of the indigenous Berber

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:20.019
people.

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:27.560
My journey of discovery begins
in Fes, Northwest Morocco,

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:31.064
the country's culinary
capital, located on the edge

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:33.466
of the Middle Atlas Mountains.

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:36.836
[music playing]

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:38.772
The medina of Fes
is one of the oldest

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:41.374
walled cities in the world.

00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:45.044
It feels like I've been
transported back in time.

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:46.946
Incredible and
beautiful and confusing

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:48.982
all at the same frickin' time.

00:00:49.048 --> 00:00:49.783
Man.

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:52.619
So.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:54.754
GORDON RAMSAY (VOICEOVER):
This place is like a labyrinth.

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:56.289
This is crazy.

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:58.258
GORDON RAMSAY (VOICEOVER):
There's over 9,000 alleyways,

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:00.760
and I think I've
been down every one.

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:02.495
The most confusing maze ever.

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:03.897
GORDON RAMSAY
(VOICEOVER): I'm supposed

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:07.367
to be meeting one of Morocco's
finest chefs, Najat Kaanache.

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:15.975
GORDON RAMSAY (VOICEOVER): But
finding our rendezvous point

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:18.311
is proving trickier
than I expected.

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:20.113
[chatter]

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:21.381
[bleep]

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:23.216
GORDON RAMSAY
(VOICEOVER): OK, I'm

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:25.452
pretty sure this is the spot.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:27.554
Oh, my god!

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:28.388
How are you?

00:01:28.455 --> 00:01:29.189
Finally.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:30.256
[music playing]

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:31.458
GORDON RAMSAY (VOICEOVER):
Najat Kaanache

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:34.360
is one of a small band of
pioneering female chefs

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:37.063
changing the face
of Moroccan cuisine.

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.465
Voila.

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:39.966
GORDON RAMSAY (VOICEOVER): After
earning her stripes at a string

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:42.869
of Michelin-star establishments
across Europe and America,

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:45.305
her own restaurant in
the heart of the medina

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:47.941
is already gaining
quite a reputation.

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:49.275
The first thing
I thought about--

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:51.110
what would it be like to have
a restaurant here with all

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:52.946
this product on your doorstep?

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:57.884
Do you ever get lost out here?

00:01:57.951 --> 00:01:58.952
You get lost.

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:00.286
Even if you live in
here, you get lost.

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:01.020
It is-- it is--

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:02.489
[both laugh]

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:03.823
So I'm not the only one.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:06.059
I get lost, and I used to
walk in this medina barefoot,

00:02:06.125 --> 00:02:06.860
so imagine.

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:07.894
In barefoot?

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:08.995
- Barefoot.
- It's so nice to met you.

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:10.296
Thank you.

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:12.966
Now I'm dying to get really
underneath this incredible

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:13.967
oasis.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:15.068
Thank you very
much for coming here.

00:02:15.134 --> 00:02:16.302
Can you lead the way,
'cause I'm useless.

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:17.270
- We go?
- OK.

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:17.770
- Can we go?
- (LAUGHING) Staight up?

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:18.738
Go on.

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:19.839
Thank you.

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:21.207
This place is crazy.

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:22.509
[music playing]

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:23.877
GORDON RAMSAY
(VOICEOVER): Najat tells

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:26.145
me that this has been a food
market since the 9th century.

00:02:31.084 --> 00:02:32.585
NAJAT KAANACHE: This is
the flavors of Morocco.

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:33.953
GORDON RAMSAY: Wow.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:34.988
NAJAT KAANACHE: Like here--
GORDON RAMSAY: Just the colors.

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:35.755
NAJAT KAANACHE:
Look at the colors.

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:36.589
GORDON RAMSAY: The colors.

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:37.557
NAJAT KAANACHE: Try this one.

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:39.058
GORDON RAMSAY: Thank you.
Mm.

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:39.926
That's delicious.

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:40.793
Chilies.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:41.928
Mm.

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:44.664
You're too whitey for
hotness, I understand.

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:46.165
I'm too white for hotness?

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:47.033
Did you just say that to me?

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:52.272
I love chilies.

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:53.373
Let's focus on this, yeah?

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:54.240
Delicious.

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:55.308
Pretty good.
Thank you.

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:56.109
Thank you.

00:02:56.175 --> 00:02:57.010
Amazing.

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:57.810
Look.

00:02:57.877 --> 00:02:58.845
Look at the meat man.

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:03.783
You like to speak French, eh?

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.118
GORDON RAMSAY: And what is that?

00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:07.921
NAJAT KAANACHE: This is the
[non-english],, Arab butter.

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:09.689
I need you to smell.

00:03:09.756 --> 00:03:10.490
Oof!

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:11.257
Bloody hell.

00:03:15.495 --> 00:03:16.496
GORDON RAMSAY: Yes.

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:17.897
I've made filo, but
that's not filo, no?

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:21.100
GORDON RAMSAY: OK, right.

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:22.068
OK.

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:23.169
It looks like my
grandma's curtains.

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:24.137
[laughs]

00:03:24.203 --> 00:03:25.705
So is it flour and water?

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:26.539
You're hilarious.

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:28.741
This is water and flour.

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:30.410
GORDON RAMSAY:
That is beautiful.

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:32.312
I think you should
go inside and try.

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:33.079
Try that?

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:34.380
Yes.

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:35.782
And if I [bleep]?

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.483
Then I'm going to
correct you with those.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:38.718
I'm allowed to do that today.

00:03:38.785 --> 00:03:39.519
Right.

00:03:39.586 --> 00:03:40.587
[laughs]

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:41.854
Will you tell her
I'm a cook in England?

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:44.591
'Cause she's looking at
me like I'm an idiot.

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:45.658
NAJAT KAANACHE: Venga, let's go.

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:46.693
[laughs]

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:47.460
GORDON RAMSAY: Ah!

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:53.566
You have to stretch
it without pressing.

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:54.667
Bravo.

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:56.102
NAJAT KAANACHE: Bravo, she says.

00:03:56.169 --> 00:03:58.371
It's so wonderful
to see you do this.

00:03:58.438 --> 00:03:59.439
Yes.

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:00.840
GORDON RAMSAY
(VOICEOVER): When Najat

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:04.377
finally stopped laughing at me,
I managed to finish my pastry.

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:06.479
NAJAT KAANACHE: Venga, stretch
it, and bring it in here, yeah?

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:07.280
Yeah.

00:04:07.347 --> 00:04:08.648
Let's go.

00:04:08.715 --> 00:04:10.416
Wow.

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:12.285
Mr. Gordon made.

00:04:12.352 --> 00:04:13.052
Bravo.

00:04:13.119 --> 00:04:14.287
[laughter]

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:15.822
Awesome.

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:17.423
Yeah, you like this more.

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:18.658
It's-- it's thin enough?

00:04:18.725 --> 00:04:21.327
So now-- hello-- now,
you have to be careful.

00:04:21.394 --> 00:04:23.129
When it cooks, you
gotta bring it up.

00:04:23.196 --> 00:04:23.963
Gotcha.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:24.864
Pick it up.

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:25.665
Oh, [bleep]!

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:27.333
Back on top a little bit.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:28.167
[speaking arabic]

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:29.802
Thank you.

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:30.603
Bravo.

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:31.671
Thank you so much.

00:04:31.738 --> 00:04:32.839
NAJAT KAANACHE: So easy.

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:34.240
E-- I wouldn't say easy.

00:04:34.307 --> 00:04:35.041
Au revoir.

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:37.143
Merci beaucoup.

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:39.779
Man, it's a lot harder than
it looks, let me tell you.

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:43.116
I'm not very good at being
crap at doing something,

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:44.951
so I felt a little bit awkward.

00:04:45.018 --> 00:04:46.152
That was difficult.

00:04:46.219 --> 00:04:48.154
Well, not difficult. It's
a lot of practice, Chef.

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:50.089
GORDON RAMSAY (VOICEOVER):
Najat is a little firecracker.

00:04:50.156 --> 00:04:52.025
That's how feisty she is.

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:53.092
Right now, I feel
like a fish out water.

